    {
      "id": "rung_main_1fb8a895-27d6-4256-a98e-4c42980d852f",
      "comment": "Stop request (seal-in latch): Stop_Cmd is a one-scan pulse, so it is remembered here until the machine reaches IDLE. Stop in IDLE does nothing. Must stay above the transitions: they read it in the same scan. The sequencer acts on it only at a safe point (Transition -> 0).",
